@startuml storage-lifecycle
!include theme.iuml
title Lifecycle acceptance preserves work and resets exercise storage
actor "Developer" as Dev
participant "Lifecycle script" as Test
participant "Editor / init container" as Editor
database "Workspace PVC" as Workspace
participant "SeaweedFS pod\nemptyDir data" as S3
Dev -> Dev : Finish workloads; export wanted outputs
Dev -> Test : Run test:lifecycle (or explicit script)
Test -> Editor : Write workspace + environment sentinels
Editor -> Workspace : Save sentinels; move environment\nto timestamped backup
Test -> S3 : Write S3 sentinel object
Test -> S3 : Replace pod and wait for readiness
note right of S3
  Old pod-local objects are discarded.
  A container-only restart can retain data.
end note
Test -> Editor : Replace editor pod
Editor -> Workspace : Preserve course files and backup;\ncreate fresh environment + kernels
Editor -> S3 : Wait for S3; initialize results bucket
Test -> Workspace : Verify retained files + backup\nand compatible new environment
Test -> S3 : Verify bucket exists; old object absent
Test -> Editor : Verify HTTP health
Test --> Dev : Lifecycle result and retained evidence
note over Workspace
  PVC keep policy is not a backup.
  Namespace / cluster deletion can destroy storage.
end note
@enduml
